    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1208" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aegyptus</span></b> , i, f., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Αἴγυπτος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>Egypt</i>, sometimes reckoned by
			the ancients as belonging to Asia: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Asiae prima pars Aegyptus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mel. 1,
					9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">proxima Africae incolitur Aegyptus, etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					5, 9, 9, § 48</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Cic. Agr. 2, 16</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Caes. B. C.
				3, 106</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Gen. 12, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">ib. Matt. 2,
				13</span></i>.</div>
